        <div class="container col-lg-9 col-sm-12 body-container color-overlay">
            <div class="row">
                <div class="col-12">
                    <div class="general-content">
                                                    <div class="body"><table style="width: 700px; height: 810px; background-color: transparent;" align="left" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="text-align: left; width: 180px; height: 220px; vertical-align: top;">
            <p><em><img alt="Stan Magidson Chair and Chief Executive Officer" src="/-/media/ASC-Publishing-Images/About-the-ASC/Executive-Management-photos/stan-magidson-web.jpg?h=220&amp;w=180&amp;hash=98624D8C17AF1AD5279CACC0A38F3DC8" style="height: 220px; width: 180px;" /></em></p>
            </td>
            <td style="text-align: left; vertical-align: top;">
            <p style="text-align: left;"><strong><span style="font-size: 18px;">Stan Magidson, KC, LLM, ICD.D</span><br />
            </strong><em>Office of the Chair and Executive Officer</em></p>
            <p style="text-align: left;">Mr. Magidson is Chair and Chief Executive Officer (CEO) of the Alberta Securities Commission and possesses extensive experience in corporate governance and securities law and regulation. Before joining the ASC in July 2016, he was President, CEO and director of the Institute of Corporate Directors and Chair of the Global Network of Director Institutes. Prior, Mr. Magidson was a partner for 21 years with a national law firm in the business law group where he advised corporate issuers, investors, financial intermediaries and boards of directors across the country on securities law, corporate finance, mergers and acquisitions and corporate governance matters. </p>
            <p style="text-align: left;">Mr. Magidson currently serves as Chair of the Canadian Securities Administrators. The CSA, the council of the securities regulators of Canada&rsquo;s provinces and territories, co-ordinates and harmonizes regulation for the Canadian capital markets.</p>
            <p style="text-align: left;">Mr. Magidson also currently serves on the international board of the Weizmann Institute of Science and the Advisory Council of Weizmann Canada. </p>
            <p style="text-align: left;">Mr. Magidson holds an LLM in Corporate Law from New York University and an LLB from the University of Ottawa.</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="text-align: left; vertical-align: top; width: 180px; height: 220px;"><img alt="Kari Horn ASC" src="/-/media/ASC-Publishing-Images/About-the-ASC/ASC-Members-photos/Kari-Horn-web.jpg?h=220&amp;w=180&amp;hash=FD6BE15A98C062C37FE92FB244467F83" style="height: 220px; width: 180px;" /></td>
            <td style="text-align: left; vertical-align: top;">
            <p><strong><span style="font-size: 18px;">Kari Horn, KC<br />
            </span></strong><em>Vice-Chair</em></p>
            <p>
            Ms. Horn was appointed Vice-Chair in May 2018. Prior to her appointment to Vice-Chair Ms. Horn was a Member of the ASC&rsquo;s senior management team as General Counsel since 2005. In this role, she led the group responsible for providing specialized legal advisory services to the Commission, staff, and market participants. She also assisted in formulation of the Commission&rsquo;s strategic policy direction and provided research and advice on emerging issues. Before joining the ASC, Ms. Horn practised securities and corporate law as a partner with a Calgary-based boutique law firm and prior to that she was as an associate at a national law firm.</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="text-align: left; vertical-align: top; width: 180px; height: 220px;">
            <p>&nbsp;<img alt="Deanna Steblyk, Vice-Chair" style="height:220px; width:180px;" src="/-/media/ASC-Publishing-Images/About-the-ASC/ASC-Members-photos/Deanna-Steblyk180x220.jpg" /></p>
            </td>
            <td style="text-align: left; vertical-align: top;">
            <p><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Deanna Steblyk, KC</strong></span><br />
            <em>Vice-Chair</em></p>
            <p>Ms. Steblyk was appointed Vice-Chair in March 2026. Prior to her appointment, Ms. Steblyk was Senior Special Counsel to the Vice-Chairs, where she assisted the Vice-Chairs and other Commissioners with their adjudicative and policy-making responsibilities. She first joined the ASC in 2008 as Senior Litigation Counsel in the Enforcement division, prosecuting breaches of Alberta securities laws before the Commission tribunal and the Alberta Provincial Court. Before joining the ASC, she practiced civil litigation primarily at two large international law firms.</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="text-align: left; vertical-align: top; width: 180px; height: 220px;"><img alt="Raymond Crossley ASC" src="/-/media/ASC-Publishing-Images/About-the-ASC/ASC-Members-photos/Raymond-Crossley-web.jpg?h=220&amp;w=180&amp;hash=976BC18DED8FB9FBC7C7F68A5EDA00F4" style="height: 220px; width: 180px;" /></td>
            <td style="text-align: left; vertical-align: top;">
            <p><strong><span style="font-size: 18px;">Raymond Crossley, FCPA, FCA, ICD.D<br />
            </span></strong><em>Lead Independent Member</em></p>
            <p>
            Mr. Crossley became a Member in April 2018 and serves as Chair of the ASC's Governance Committee. He is a highly experienced financial professional and corporate director with strong management and governance skills. In addition to his role with the ASC, Mr. Crossley currently serves on the board of directors of Obsidian Energy Ltd. Most recently, he was Chief Financial Officer of the Calgary Health Foundation before retiring in 2023. Mr. Crossley previously served as Managing Partner, Western Canada for PwC Canada and was the audit partner on a broad range of public companies primarily in the energy sector. He has served on other corporate and not-for-profit boards and as a member of the ASC&rsquo;s Financial Review Committee and the Financial Advisory Committee. Mr. Crossley holds the ICD.D designation from the Institute of Corporate Directors and is a member of the Institute of Chartered Professional Accountants of Alberta. He graduated from the University of Western Ontario with a degree in Economics and Political Science.&nbsp;            </p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="text-align: left; vertical-align: top; width: 180px; height: 220px;"><img height="220" alt="  Matthew Bootle, FCA" width="180" src="/-/media/ASC-Publishing-Images/About-the-ASC/ASC-Members-photos/Matthew-Bootle_crop_web180x220.jpg?h=220&amp;w=180&amp;hash=45ADCE517BA521E5DA70B64205EEF63C" style="height: 220px; width: 180px;" /></td>
            <td style="text-align: left; vertical-align: top;">
            <p><strong><span style="font-size: 18px;">Matthew Bootle, FCA</span></strong></p>
            <p>Mr. Bootle became a Member in April 2019 and serves on the ASC&rsquo;s Audit Committee. A retired partner with Ernst &amp; Young LLP, Mr. Bootle has over 30 years of experience as a financial and legal professional. He is a former Director of Accounting Standards and Director of Policy at the TSX Venture Exchange and returns to the ASC where he served as Chief Accountant from 1993 to 1997. Mr. Bootle is a Fellow of the Chartered Professional Accountants of Alberta (CPA Alberta) and received a CPA Alberta Distinguished Service Award in 2012, and a CPA Alberta Lifetime Achievement Award in 2025. He received a Bachelor of Commerce, Bachelor of Laws and Master&rsquo;s degree in Adult Education from the University of Calgary.</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="text-align: left; vertical-align: top; width: 180px; height: 220px;"><img height="220" alt="Gail Harding, Q.C., ICD.D" width="180" src="/-/media/ASC-Publishing-Images/About-the-ASC/ASC-Members-photos/Gail-Harding_web180x220.jpg" /></td>
            <td style="text-align: left; vertical-align: top;">
            <p><strong><span style="font-size: 18px;">Gail Harding, KC, ICD.D</span></strong></p>
            <p>
            <span>Ms. Harding became a Member in April 2019 and serves on the ASC&rsquo;s Human Resources Committee. Ms. Harding&nbsp; has over 30 years of experience as a financial services executive and corporate lawyer.&nbsp;</span>She currently serves as Chair of the Board of Meridian Credit Union and is a former director of Pieridae Energy Limited.  Ms. Harding previously served as Senior Vice President, Chief Legal Officer and Corporate Secretary at Canadian Western Bank Financial Group. A prior member of the C.D. Howe Financial Services Research Council, she is a recipient of the Canadian General Counsel Award &ndash; Mid-Market Excellence and the Women in Law Leadership Award. Ms. Harding received a Bachelor of Education and a Bachelor of Laws from the University of Alberta, a Master of Laws (specialization in Energy and Infrastructure) from York University and holds the ICD.D designation.</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="text-align: left; vertical-align: top; width: 180px; height: 220px;"><img alt="ASC commission member evan hazell" style="height:220px; width:180px;" src="/-/media/ASC-Publishing-Images/About-the-ASC/ASC-Members-photos/Commission-Member_Evan-Hazell_Profile-photo.jpg?h=220&amp;w=180&amp;hash=ADA8ABC289BCEB382D0519B1767BFEBB" /><br />
            </td>
            <td style="text-align: left; vertical-align: top;"><strong><span style="font-size: 18px;">Evan Hazell, P.Eng.&nbsp;</span></strong>
            <p>Mr. Hazell became a Member in July 2026 and serves on the ASC&rsquo;s Governance Committee. He brings a breadth of experience with more than 30 years in the global energy industry, first as a petroleum engineer and later as an investment banker specializing in the oil and gas industry. He served as a managing director at several financial institutions, including HSBC Global Investment Bank and RBC Capital Markets. For the past 15 years, Mr. Hazell has been active as a corporate director with various domestic and international organizations, as well as a range of community organizations.&nbsp; Mr. Hazell holds a Master of Engineering degree from the University of Calgary and a Master of Business Administration from the University of Michigan.</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="text-align: left; vertical-align: top; width: 180px; height: 220px;"><img alt="ASC commission member richard jones " style="height:220px; width:180px;" src="/-/media/ASC-Publishing-Images/About-the-ASC/ASC-Members-photos/Richard-Jones_180x220.jpg" /></td>
            <td style="text-align: left; vertical-align: top;">
            <p><strong><span style="font-size: 18px;">C. Richard Jones, KC&nbsp;</span></strong></p>
            <p>Mr. Jones became a Member in July 2026 and serves on the ASC&rsquo;s Human Resources Committee. He is a highly accomplished lawyer with more than 30 years of experience and is currently with Brownlee LLP. Previously, he practiced with two national law firms and was a founding partner of a commercial litigation boutique. Throughout his career, he has helped public- and private-sector clients navigate complex regulatory landscapes, manage legal risk and address multifaceted matters. His practice encompasses corporate and commercial law, environmental law, municipal law, and natural resource development. Mr. Jones holds an LLB from the University of Calgary and serves as a Director with the Canadian Bitcoin Consortium.</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="text-align: left; vertical-align: top; width: 180px; height: 220px;"><img alt="Karen Kim ASC" src="/-/media/ASC-Publishing-Images/About-the-ASC/ASC-Members-photos/Karen-Kim-web.jpg?h=220&amp;w=180&amp;hash=69111D524788B5CD258FE69EF92FBC61" style="height: 220px; width: 180px;" /></td>
            <td style="text-align: left; vertical-align: top;">
            <p><strong><span style="font-size: 18px;">Karen Kim, CPA, CA, CFA, ICD.D</span></strong></p>
            <p>
            Ms. Kim became a Member in May 2017 and serves as the Chair of the ASC&rsquo;s Audit Committee. She possesses over 25 years of experience in capital markets, derivatives, risk management and investments. She has worked in progressively more senior finance roles at Petro-Canada and Suncor Energy. Ms. Kim is also a Public member of the Audit Committee for the City of Calgary. She holds a B.Comm (Accounting) from the University of Calgary, and is a Chartered Professional Accountant and Chartered Financial Analyst. Ms. Kim also holds the ICD.D designation from the Institute of Corporate Directors.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="text-align: left; vertical-align: top; width: 180px; height: 220px;"><img height="220" alt="Doug Mair" width="180" src="/-/media/ASC-Publishing-Images/About-the-ASC/ASC-Members-photos/Doug-Mair-web.jpg" /></td>
            <td style="text-align: left; vertical-align: top;">
            <p><strong><span style="font-size: 18px;">Doug Mair, ICD.D</span></strong></p>
            <p>
            Mr. Mair became a Member in April 2021 and serves on the ASC&rsquo;s Human Resources Committee. He has over 35 years of experience in the investment industry and is currently with Richardson Wealth Limited. He has a wide range of experience in virtually every segment of the investment industry. Mr. Mair was a founding member of Richardson Partners Financial Ltd. and served on the board for four years, and has served on numerous boards in a variety of private corporations and not-for-profit organizations. Mr. Mair has been a Fellow of the Canadian Securities Institute for over 20 years and holds the ICD.D designation from the Institute of Corporate Directors. Mr. Mair graduated from Queen&rsquo;s University with a degree in Economics and History.</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="text-align: left; vertical-align: top; width: 180px; height: 220px;"><img alt="ASC commission member Linda Thomas" style="height:220px; width:180px;" src="/-/media/ASC-Publishing-Images/About-the-ASC/ASC-Members-photos/Linda-Thomas_180x220.jpg" /><br />
            </td>
            <td style="text-align: left; vertical-align: top;">
            <p><strong><span style="font-size: 18px;">Linda Thomas, ICD.D&nbsp;</span></strong></p>
            <p>Ms. Thomas became a Member in July 2026 and serves on the ASC&rsquo;s Audit Committee. She is a seasoned business executive with more than 30 years of experience across telecommunications, technology and consumer packaged goods. Most recently, she served as Senior Vice-President, Commercial Finance at Shaw/Rogers Communications. Throughout her career, she has held leadership roles spanning numerous disciplines including finance, strategy, transformation, product management, marketing and supply chain, with expertise in finance and audit, and mergers and acquisitions. Ms. Thomas is an experienced corporate director and she currently serves on the board of Big Rock Brewery Inc., where she chairs the Audit Committee and sits on other committees. She is also a Senator and Executive Committee member with the University of Calgary Senate. She holds an Honours Bachelor of Mathematics from the University of Waterloo and the ICD.D designation and has completed executive education through the Institute of Corporate Directors, Harvard Executive Education and The Banff Centre.&nbsp;</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="text-align: left; vertical-align: top; width: 180px; height: 220px;">
            <p><img src="/-/media/ASC-Publishing-Images/About-the-ASC/ASC-Members-photos/BryceTingle-4web-180x220.jpg" style="height:220px; width:180px;" alt="Bryce Tingle " /></p>
            </td>
            <td style="text-align: left; vertical-align: top;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Bryce C. Tingle, KC,&nbsp;LLB, LLM</strong></span><br />
            <p>Mr. Tingle became a Member in May 2022 and serves on the ASC&rsquo;s Governance Committee. He has more than 30 years experience as a corporate finance lawyer, initially in private practice, then as the general counsel of large internationally-focused technology and energy companies. He holds the N. Murray Edwards Chair in Business Law at the University of Calgary and currently serves as the board chair of several private technology and asset management companies. He is one of the four members of the National Special Advisory Group for the Integrated Market Enforcement Team of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police. Mr. Tingle has been Director of the Financial Markets Regulation Programme at the University of Calgary&rsquo;s School of Public Policy, a member of the Ontario Securities Commission&rsquo;s Exempt Markets Committee and the ASC&rsquo;s Securities Advisory Committee. He has law degrees from the University of Alberta, Osgoode Hall and Duke University and was twice named one of the University of Calgary&rsquo;s peak scholars. Mr. Tingle&rsquo;s academic research focuses on corporate governance and entrepreneurial law.
            </p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="text-align: left; vertical-align: top; width: 180px; height: 220px;"><img src="/-/media/ASC-Publishing-Images/About-the-ASC/ASC-Members-photos/AndreaWhyte_180x220.jpg" style="height:220px; width:180px;" alt="Andrea Whyte" /></td>
            <td style="text-align: left; vertical-align: top;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><strong>Andrea Whyte, KC, LLB</strong></span><br />
            <p>Ms. Whyte became a Member in November 2024 and serves as Chair of the ASC&rsquo;s Human Resources Committee. She has over 25 years of experience as a corporate lawyer with a focus on corporate securities, mergers and acquisitions and corporate governance. In addition to her role with the ASC, Ms. Whyte is currently a senior partner at Osler, Hoskin &amp; Harcourt LLP and serves on the board of directors of Maxim Power Corp. and she is a former director of Westbrick Energy Ltd. Ms. Whyte is also a member of Osler&rsquo;s national partnership board and a member of Osler&rsquo;s Audit, Finance &amp; Risk Committee. Ms. Whyte holds a B.Sc. from McGill University and a law degree from the University of Alberta.</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
